    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Kyle Tucker** (81.26), both of whom benefit significantly from facing favorable starting pitching matchups against Littell and Kochanowicz, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** remains our most potent asset, drawing a +18% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s xERA of 4.73 and maintaining his lead-off spot. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** is positioned to capitalize on a high-ceiling matchup where the pitcher\u2019s skill deficiencies and a favorable park environment significantly inflate his scoring potential. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.73) and **Jackson Merrill** (68.69) also present strong value; both are benefiting from the 14% and 13% efficiency boosts provided by their respective platoon advantages against right-handed starters, with **Jackson Merrill** providing elite sprint speed utility that remains a primary focus of our roster construction.\n\nThe decision to bench **Coby Mayo** (49.85) was the most difficult call of the morning, as he hovered just below our target threshold of 50.0. While **Coby Mayo** benefits from the same favorable park environment as **Gunnar Henderson**, his projected spot in the 8-hole and a negative platoon adjustment caused by the opposing righty arm pushed him behind **Brady House** (56.25) and **Sam Antonacci** (54.85). **Sam Antonacci** is particularly interesting today, as his elite xwOBA of 0.403 helps mitigate the relative difficulty of facing Cabrera, justifying his inclusion over lower-ceiling bench bats like **Miguel Vargas** (47.43) or **Nolan Schanuel** (46.41).\n\nWe remain cautious regarding the risks inherent in today's slate, specifically concerning **Heliot Ramos**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Josh Lowe**. All three are operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status; should their actual batting orders drop significantly, their daily efficiency scores will fluctuate. Furthermore, while we have loaded the lineup with hitters optimized against right-handed pitching, **Drake Baldwin** faces a difficult task against Early, with a stiff -19% penalty applied due to the SP\u2019s elite 2.92 xERA. We will monitor weather and final lineup cards closely to ensure that our total game caps are not exhausted by low-efficiency starts.",
